{
  "about": "Composer and multi-line prompt editing (D29, features composer and multiline): the same key handling in every client. keys are canonical key names (core-protocol.md, Keys) applied in order; `paste:<text>` inserts text as a paste; `set:<arg>=<value>` chooses a control value (client-local until Send). expect.outcomes is each key's result (edit, submit, leave, refused, ignored); text and cursor (a character index) are the final state; args is what Send invokes the row's command with, after the last submit (null if none). Enter sends; Shift-Enter, Alt-Enter and Ctrl-J add a line; submit: \"C-Enter\" swaps them. max_bytes counts UTF-8 bytes; a paste over it is refused whole. Generated by the Rust model (tests/client_conformance.rs, VQRO_FIXTURE_UPDATE=1) and reviewed.",
